# Dependent variable in Y = b0 + b1*X + U
# Y

# What the error term U represents
# Factors OTHER than X that affect Y

# What the slope b1 measures
# The ceteris paribus effect of X on Y (change in Y per one-unit rise in X, holding other factors fixed)

# Zero conditional mean assumption E[U|X] = 0
# The average of U does not depend on X

# Conditional mean E[Y|X=x] under SLR with E[U|X] = 0
# b0 + b1*x

# How the OLS slope estimate b1-hat can be written
# cov(x, y) / var(x)

# Why we must ESTIMATE b0 and b1
# They are population quantities; we observe only a sample

# What the term b0 + b1*X is
# The part of Y EXPLAINED by X (its conditional mean)

